= MediaWiki =

'''MediaWiki''' is open-source wiki software designed for collaborative, revisioned hypertext publishing. It provides pages, namespaces, templates, transclusion, parser functions, revision history, permissions, APIs, content models, categories, files, and an extension architecture.

Wikipedia is the best-known MediaWiki deployment, but MediaWiki is a general platform rather than a Wikipedia-specific content model.

== Programmability ==

MediaWiki can be extended at several layers. Templates and parser functions provide declarative/reusable wikitext behavior. Extensions add PHP-side capabilities, parser hooks, APIs, special pages, storage models, namespaces, and integrations. [[Scribunto]] embeds [[Lua]] modules for reusable procedural computation.

MediaWiki's page and revision model also provides a durable substrate for systems that treat pages as more than static documents: pages can carry structured annotations, invoke computations, transclude canonical matter, and expose multiple dynamically computed views.

== MediaWiki in BITwiki ==

BITwiki uses MediaWiki as its durable knowledge execution substrate. The wiki provides canonical pages and revisions; [[Semantic MediaWiki]] provides graph/property semantics; [[Cargo (MediaWiki extension)|Cargo]] provides repeated operational records; Scribunto/Lua provides deterministic transformation and semantic presentation.

The architecture is documented at [[BITwiki:MediaWiki substrate]] and [[BITwiki:Programmable knowledge substrate]].

[[BIThub]] is the Discourse-based interaction/workflow plane around this durable layer. Humans and agents can research, discuss, coordinate, and propose changes through BIThub while stable knowledge is represented in MediaWiki. Cross-system transport belongs to explicit integration APIs/plugins/services rather than to page-level Lua code.

